{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "03B2", "placeholders": {"QUOTECLOSE_0001": "''", "QUOTEOPEN_0001": "``"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e0f1f90cdc3e44f9ffec8efa70f662f559790c3840c8ec88de7a077d2a7a3989", "source_text": "Mumford never uses the term <QUOTEOPEN_0001>stack<QUOTECLOSE_0001> here but the concept is implicit in the paper; he computes the picard group of the moduli stack of elliptic curves.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cd14dd8c821605f66218fdde717d72bda20c997869c51ebc0d946e5d5083fc6a", "unit_id": "tag:03B2:item001-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "03B2", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Deligne, Mumford: \\emph{", "suffix": "} \\cite{DM}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0e0080609a0d1f131a6b9d6c21ebfda5dc55ce689a55d566d1c2375eac0c3ec7", "source_text": "The irreducibility of the space of curves of given genus", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0f83492b6d9fcd08a0a2e3b7906ad2685820d97ee48fa2bf3e69b2b90ac023f6", "unit_id": "tag:03B2:item002"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "03B2", "placeholders": {"EMPHCLOSE_0001": "}", "EMPHOPEN_0001": "\\emph{", "LATIN_0001": "\\'etale", "MATH_0001": "$g$", "QUOTECLOSE_0001": "''", "QUOTEOPEN_0001": "``"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:973fbcb42139f4e15582a3e4655c9a86463f57cc7032f8722d288e1595bcaa2b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:980036cec415b63c91d4cde4a83079c33ad2ec0a0fcdde2c0b50860cc398f02d", "source_text": "This influential paper introduces <QUOTEOPEN_0001>algebraic stacks<QUOTECLOSE_0001> in the sense which are now universally called Deligne-Mumford stacks (stacks with representable diagonal which admit <LATIN_0001> presentations by schemes). There are many foundational results <EMPHOPEN_0001>without proof<EMPHCLOSE_0001>. The paper uses stacks to give two proofs of the irreducibility of the moduli space of curves of genus <MATH_0001>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e385b4f8648b4cafbcccbedc32b51188617ff51de87655180f2f17007509d992", "unit_id": "tag:03B2:item002-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "03B2", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Artin: \\emph{", "suffix": "}\n\\cite{ArtinVersal}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:749ebc0d8b3b687c2b2019bdf42404fd494cf6072fbf2e839ac2e36c901d836b", "source_text": "Versal deformations and algebraic stacks", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5446f3d5931d8ec6079e8a6c139ec250a70aada03ef7469b78121d1bd6bbb715", "unit_id": "tag:03B2:item003"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "03B2", "placeholders": {"EMPHCLOSE_0001": "}", "EMPHOPEN_0001": "\\emph{", "QUOTECLOSE_0001": "''", "QUOTEOPEN_0001": "``"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n\\end{itemize}\n\n\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0c1f21ef8370e931cb6b2913d7cb99845a21b3108491a3f1573edc56b517f238", "source_text": "This paper introduces <QUOTEOPEN_0001>algebraic stacks<QUOTECLOSE_0001> which generalize Deligne-Mumford stacks and are now commonly referred to as <EMPHOPEN_0001>Artin stacks<EMPHCLOSE_0001>, stacks with representable diagonal which admit smooth presentations by schemes. This paper gives deformation-theoretic criterion known as Artin's criterion which allows one to prove that a given moduli stack is an Artin stack without explicitly exhibiting a presentation.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0cd768e36a3706e119d9a82b85c043d62578c246e853c8d996e901e38b8b0fd9", "unit_id": "tag:03B2:item003-quote"}
